<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantin of Rostov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1186–1218</span> · Also known as Konstantin Vsevolodovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantin Vsevolodovich was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a>, prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostov">Rostov</a> and, after defeating his brothers at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lipitsa">Battle of Lipitsa</a> in 1216, Grand Prince of Vladimir until his death in 1218. Before he died he divided the Rostov lands among his sons, creating the separate principalities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslavl">Yaroslavl</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uglich">Uglich</a> and Rostov.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstantin-of-rostov.jpg" alt="Konstantin of Rostov" width="320" height="513" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian painter (1670s-1917) Public domain image (according to PD-Russia-expired) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archangel_Cathedral_-_NE_column,_1st_lev.,_south_-_Konstantin_Vsevolodovich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
